WEBVTT

00:01:29.263 --> 00:01:31.597
For us, when we're confronted
with information

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.063
that challenges an existing worldview,

00:01:35.097 --> 00:01:38.830
our tendency is not to open up,
it's to double down.

00:01:38.863 --> 00:01:41.463
We even have a term for it
in social psychology.

00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:44.263
It's called belief perseverance.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:49.463
And boy, do some people's beliefs
seem to persevere.

00:01:50.363 --> 00:01:53.563
I'm no stranger to tough conversations.

00:01:53.597 --> 00:01:56.997
I got my start in what I now call
productive disagreement

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:58.430
in high school debate.

00:01:58.463 --> 00:01:59.763
I even went on to win

00:01:59.797 --> 00:02:02.897
the World Schools Debate
Championship three times.